{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1382725-decent-anshega","id":1382725,"title":"Decent Anshega","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-20T05:49:20-07:00","id":1382725,"title":"Decent Anshega","content":"Does anyone have any ideas for Pure Uratha that are decent people? As good as or possibly better than the Forsaken are?<br /> I know it's possible because I went out of my way to build a Pure pack that were decent (it's the core of one of the plot hooks I put up on the werewolf plot hooks thread). Just wondering if anyone else has ideas they want to share.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T06:40:52-07:00","id":1382737,"title":"","content":"Well, by default the Pure are devoted to bizarre beliefs, but are not psycho-killers, obviously they despise uratha but i would not define them as the bad guys.<br /> A fire touched could be a disciple of a wealth spirit, who told him to earn lot of money to distribute to poor people, making them more Resonant.<br /> A predator king could be a hermit who refuses any kind of violence not finalized to the hunt, and he coul teach homeless people how to better survive moving in a more rural areas.<br /> A ivory claw could be a lawyer who &quot;hunts&quot; parents that abuse their children, and live a simple life caring for his family","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T07:01:37-07:00","id":1382744,"title":"","content":"I can think of a Pure Uratha who's a decent person. One who stops being a Pure.<br /> <br /> THe best you're gonna have are the FIre-touched, who can be some of the nicest people you'll ever meet, but do use plague and madness to slowly tear apart anyone who doesn't join their cult.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T08:35:19-07:00","id":1382763,"title":"","content":"Ivory Claws that believe no one should be able to hunt among their herd and really push the familial honor thing. It can be taken a bad way but it could easily be an extension of some existing leaders ethos'. For instance in the core you have Ivory Claw packs in Holmes County that arbitrated a peace between warring Pure and Forsaken because they were paying attention to a bigger picture (multiple times). Fire-Touched are big on their religion of the Shadow and that doesn't have to be bad for their congregation. Even a Predator King has no reason to be a jerk to you unless you're dishonoring his beliefs first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-20-2020, 11:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T10:01:03-07:00","id":1382782,"title":"","content":"Consider that each of the Forsaken are also part of a murder-cult to ancient Wolf gods and use fear, savage fury, and systematic destruction of people's social relationships in order to kill their prey efficiently and completely. And then realize there's some decent people in there as well. Even the Pure need to cleave to humans and have friends and family. They might even be the kinds of Werewolves that work to foster a healthy community to everyone's benefit. Ivory Claws could be philanthropists, Fire-Touched could be therapists, Predator Kings could hunt poachers. <br /> <br /> Of course the natural state of a Werewolf is usually far from what we'd call &quot;decent&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25423-voytek","name":"Voytek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25423_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T17:35:35-07:00","id":1382857,"title":"","content":"I've decided to go over the decent Pure that I came up with here.<br /> <br /> Fire-Touched: believes that to properly make the decision between being joining the Pure &amp; joining the Forsaken, one must know all sides to a story.<br /> He regularly volunteers to tell the stories, myths, &amp; legends of the Uratha people whomever will listen, with the understanding that he will not limit himself to one sides interpretation.<br /> <br /> Ivory Claw: the purity that the Ivory Claw believes in is purity of motive &amp; of purpose.<br /> This has resulted in him going after police who abuse their authority when they should be doing their job &quot;serve &amp; protect&quot;, as well as rapists who claim they rape because of lust or because &quot;she was asking for it&quot;.<br /> He is honest about what he does &amp; why he does it when asked.<br /> <br /> Predator King: The Predator King is the alpha of this pack. He is very strong on a physical level but is fundamentally aware of his own limitations.<br /> He is aware that the territory he currently has is bordering on the absolute limit of what he can control &amp; actively avoids reaching for more. He also maintains positive relations with the local Forsaken packs, helping ensure that he doesn't have to worry about his borders as much &amp; can focus more attention on potential foes &amp; threats coming from inside his territory.<br /> <br /> I apologize for making all three of them guys. I unfortunately did that on reflex. With that in mind, I do not consider their gender identities or physical gender to be set in stone if anyone wants to use them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T19:06:49-07:00","id":1382872,"title":"","content":"In the previous post, when I bring up &quot;physical gender&quot; I am referring to what equipment they/you/etc. have.<br /> If anyone decides to make the argument that with the Wolf Gift Luna's Embrace anyone can correct themselves so that the external &amp; the internal match, I say, that yes anyone can, doesn't mean everyone will.<br /> There are a number of reasons why an Uratha wouldn't use Luna's Embrace including denial &amp; social circumstances won't allow for it. One reason why the Pure specifically wouldn't use it is the name, it's called Luna's Embrace.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T23:48:47-07:00","id":1382914,"title":"","content":"Just make a decent person and then make them Pure.<br /> <br /> Like, a survivalist Predator King who is an isolationist/survivalist but not a monster. Or a conservationist. The only requirement is that they respect the hunt, and honour nothing of human craft (which has a wide variation of interpretations. One PK might just not buy anything but practical items - nothing *special* - they're just things, one might make everything himself, one might consider honour to mean 'rely', one might interpret it to mean 'value'.<br /> <br /> Fire-touched are easy. Just make a priest and give him slightly weirder beliefs, or a pious man, or a missionary, or a congregant.<br /> <br /> Ivory Claw might be the easiest. Just make their purity angle more about family than racism and you're good. Family is everything. Think Fast and the Furious, Mafia/Yakuza, Italian Grandmothers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T02:09:29-07:00","id":1382930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1382725-decent-anshega?p=1382914#post1382914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just make a decent person and then make them Pure.<br /> <br /> Like, a survivalist Predator King who is an isolationist/survivalist but not a monster. Or a conservationist. The only requirement is that they respect the hunt, and honour nothing of human craft (which has a wide variation of interpretations. One PK might just not buy anything but practical items - nothing *special* - they're just things, one might make everything himself, one might consider honour to mean 'rely', one might interpret it to mean 'value'.<br /> <br /> Fire-touched are easy. Just make a priest and give him slightly weirder beliefs, or a pious man, or a missionary, or a congregant.<br /> <br /> Ivory Claw might be the easiest. Just make their purity angle more about family than racism and you're good. Family is everything. Think Fast and the Furious, Mafia/Yakuza, Italian Grandmothers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, i m italian and thanks to you now i can t stop imagining my 80 years grandma as a ferocious werewolf armed with a wooden slipper","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T02:37:34-07:00","id":1382934,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26055\" data-vbnamecard=\"26055\">Krat05</a> I like all three of your characters. If I played an Uratha (either a Forsaken or another Anshega), I could totally see her listening to the Fire-Touched tell stories, crushing on the Ivory Claw (from a distance; the Litany wouldn\u2019t let her get too close) and maybe bonding over hunting experiences with the Predator King.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T03:21:57-07:00","id":1382938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1382725-decent-anshega?p=1382934#post1382934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> I like all three of your characters. If I played an Uratha (either a Forsaken or another Anshega), I could totally see her listening to the Fire-Touched tell stories, crushing on the Ivory Claw (from a distance; the Litany wouldn\u2019t let her get too close) and maybe bonding over hunting experiences with the Predator King.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks.<br /> The road to their creation was long &amp; twisted according to my memory. In creating them, I wasn't just trying to make Pure that were decent people, I was trying to make Pure that Forsaken packs could happily work with &amp; create conflict when more regular Pure or Forsaken turned up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T05:06:20-07:00","id":1382956,"title":"","content":"I think it\u2019s a fantastic idea. Hope your players like your Pure characters as much as I did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T13:55:20-07:00","id":1383435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krat05</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1382725-decent-anshega?p=1382857#post1382857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've decided to go over the decent Pure that I came up with here.<br /> <br /> Fire-Touched: believes that to properly make the decision between being joining the Pure &amp; joining the Forsaken, one must know all sides to a story.<br /> He regularly volunteers to tell the stories, myths, &amp; legends of the Uratha people whomever will listen, with the understanding that he will not limit himself to one sides interpretation.<br /> <br /> Ivory Claw: the purity that the Ivory Claw believes in is purity of motive &amp; of purpose.<br /> This has resulted in him going after police who abuse their authority when they should be doing their job &amp;quot;serve &amp; protect&amp;quot;, as well as rapists who claim they rape because of lust or because &amp;quot;she was asking for it&amp;quot;.<br /> He is honest about what he does &amp; why he does it when asked.<br /> <br /> Predator King: The Predator King is the alpha of this pack. He is very strong on a physical level but is fundamentally aware of his own limitations.<br /> He is aware that the territory he currently has is bordering on the absolute limit of what he can control &amp; actively avoids reaching for more. He also maintains positive relations with the local Forsaken packs, helping ensure that he doesn't have to worry about his borders as much &amp; can focus more attention on potential foes &amp; threats coming from inside his territory.<br /> <br /> I apologize for making all three of them guys. I unfortunately did that on reflex. With that in mind, I do not consider their gender identities or physical gender to be set in stone if anyone wants to use them.</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems nearly everyone on this thread has misunderstood a few things or are subtly redefining what the Pure stand for.<br /> <br /> The Fire-touched are devoted to truth and dogma, an irreconcilable contradiction for the sane. Hence the madness.<br /> <br /> The Ivory Claws are into eugenics. That is what &quot;purity&quot; means. They are all but nazis.<br /> <br /> Predator Kings are about the strong dominating the weak and the collapse of civilization. <br /> <br /> And finally hatred and genocide tie them all together. This is all undeniable there and yet you ripped out the context and added your own definitions. If you explore decency in the Pure just know it is the same as exploring goodness in someone raised in a hate group, these details shouldn't be ignored.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T14:05:46-07:00","id":1383436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1382725-decent-anshega?p=1383435#post1383435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems nearly everyone on this thread has misunderstood a few things or are subtly redefining what the Pure stand for.<br /> <br /> ....<br /> <br /> And finally hatred and genocide tie them all together. This is all undeniable there and yet you ripped out the context and added your own definitions. If you explore decency in the Pure just know it is the same as exploring goodness in someone raised in a hate group, these details shouldn't be ignored.</div> </div> </div> </div>They changed a bit across editions. Shifts of focus that make them less torch-bearing evil goons across the board. You can still play them that way but they're not as limited by that. As shown by the examples in the second edition books, and the Pure sections. And the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/playing-the-pure-werewolf-the-forsaken/\" target=\"_blank\">Playing the Pure blog</a> which was included in a Dark Era book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T14:19:37-07:00","id":1383438,"title":"","content":"I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T14:42:37-07:00","id":1383445,"title":"","content":"I mean every tribe looks &quot;evil&quot; when you describe them in broad enough strokes. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25423-voytek","name":"Voytek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25423_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T22:03:34-07:00","id":1383508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Voytek</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1382725-decent-anshega?p=1383445#post1383445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean every tribe looks &quot;evil&quot; when you describe them in broad enough strokes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like this misses the forest for the trees.<br /> <br /> Broadly speaking, the franchise's use of monsters as a lens for humanity tends to mean that the individual character types are kind of default sort of grey as that entire moral black and white morality scale goes, with individual players deciding how to brighten up or darken down on their deicisons, which often sets a tone for the conflict.<br /> <br /> As a result of that grey nature to of everything, larger organizations of the monsters tend to conglomerate around those grey concepts, mixtures of positives that are also paired with negatives that reflect the thematic concerns and common answers to those concerns in a way that are generally morally and ethically conflicting (nevermind the larger tendency that while these organization tends to give monsters a form of community where they can be themselves, they also tend to increase the incentives to dive into further monstrosity)-conflicting enough that they make for evocative characters and set pieces for certain kinds of stories, but also arguably justified and even beneficient enough in their way. They look evil in the broad stokes because they are Monstrous Organizations and Monsters are Some Kind of Strife for Humanity to a Human Perspective(and they often have a right to say such, Hunter's aren't devoid of justifable monstrosity)<br /> <br /> The Antagonist Organizations, by contrast (in all but....one and a half and a half cases) are there as something of a crystal clear message of what is meant to be Too Far down the monstrous scale, where it stops being a matter of your circumstances and a clear case of being an asshole. They are a set black to contrast all that grey up above against. You may be a monster, you may be Some Kind of Strife, and the way you deal with that may be Some Kind of Questionable, but these guys are the Line In The Sand, the point where you go from kinda iffy to Absolute Fucktard. Let's not sugarcoat in, outside of the odd exceptions, these organizations of monsters tend to reflect some of the clearest evils we see in the real world, unabashedly. Individuals may be in them for what are much more conflicted reasons, but the organizations themselves are <i>supposed</i> to be a clear evil.<br /> <br /> This is kind of why I feel like &quot;Decent Anshega&quot; and &quot;Good Seers of the Throne&quot; miss the point. Yes, we want characters to be believable and going for a sympathetic approach where in we approach the motivations of the antagonists rationally is a way of doing that, but it misses both the point that these aren't organizations that appeal to people with a mind towards communal decency and personal moral and ethical standing, and often they don't appeal to rational argumentation.<br /> <br /> The Pure are werewolves motivated by hatred of the world and what they got, they hearken back to a myth that doesn't reflect the realities of either the present or the days those myths took place in because it gives them a feeling of power and place. They are motivated by a sense that civilization has castrated them, that their racial superiority and purity is being defiled by interbreeding, that their religions justify their violence against an unworthy and unenlightened mass. These things will never make logical or rational sense, and certainly defy any sense of actual moral or ethical consideration, but because their feelings on this feeds their sense of identity and capacity for action, they will dive head first into and cling to it. At best, you might be able to have something like civil conversation with them-hell, the Fire-touched <i>love</i> it when you buy into that -but at the end of the day, these are people who would gladly support action to kill you because it makes them feel good and right and in a place they belong that is them and theirs if they weren't werewolves for anything any reasonable and rational person would clearly see as <i>wrong</i>-and since they <i>are</i> werewolves, they don't just have to support it, they can and will take action to those ends.<br /> <br /> That the Forsaken also kill humans and willfully shape territories in ways that is demonstrably monstrous does not make the Pure an equal form of evil to them. They clearly embody ideologies and practices that are far more reprehensible than the murky waters the Forsaken exist and act in.<br /> <br /> The only decent Pure is an Uratha who <i>stops being a Pure</i>. Anything else is just killing you with a smile.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T23:11:56-07:00","id":1383515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1382725-decent-anshega?p=1383508#post1383508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like this misses the forest for the trees.<br /> <br /> Broadly speaking, the franchise's use of monsters as a lens for humanity tends to mean that the individual character types are kind of default sort of grey as that entire moral black and white morality scale goes, with individual players deciding how to brighten up or darken down on their deicisons, which often sets a tone for the conflict.<br /> <br /> As a result of that grey nature to of everything, larger organizations of the monsters tend to conglomerate around those grey concepts, mixtures of positives that are also paired with negatives that reflect the thematic concerns and common answers to those concerns in a way that are generally morally and ethically conflicting (nevermind the larger tendency that while these organization tends to give monsters a form of community where they can be themselves, they also tend to increase the incentives to dive into further monstrosity)-conflicting enough that they make for evocative characters and set pieces for certain kinds of stories, but also arguably justified and even beneficient enough in their way. They look evil in the broad stokes because they are Monstrous Organizations and Monsters are Some Kind of Strife for Humanity to a Human Perspective(and they often have a right to say such, Hunter's aren't devoid of justifable monstrosity)<br /> <br /> The Antagonist Organizations, by contrast (in all but....one and a half and a half cases) are there as something of a crystal clear message of what is meant to be Too Far down the monstrous scale, where it stops being a matter of your circumstances and a clear case of being an asshole. They are a set black to contrast all that grey up above against. You may be a monster, you may be Some Kind of Strife, and the way you deal with that may be Some Kind of Questionable, but these guys are the Line In The Sand, the point where you go from kinda iffy to Absolute Fucktard. Let's not sugarcoat in, outside of the odd exceptions, these organizations of monsters tend to reflect some of the clearest evils we see in the real world, unabashedly. Individuals may be in them for what are much more conflicted reasons, but the organizations themselves are <i>supposed</i> to be a clear evil.<br /> <br /> This is kind of why I feel like &amp;quot;Decent Anshega&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;Good Seers of the Throne&amp;quot; miss the point. Yes, we want characters to be believable and going for a sympathetic approach where in we approach the motivations of the antagonists rationally is a way of doing that, but it misses both the point that these aren't organizations that appeal to people with a mind towards communal decency and personal moral and ethical standing, and often they don't appeal to rational argumentation.<br /> <br /> The Pure are werewolves motivated by hatred of the world and what they got, they hearken back to a myth that doesn't reflect the realities of either the present or the days those myths took place in because it gives them a feeling of power and place. They are motivated by a sense that civilization has castrated them, that their racial superiority and purity is being defiled by interbreeding, that their religions justify their violence against an unworthy and unenlightened mass. These things will never make logical or rational sense, and certainly defy any sense of actual moral or ethical consideration, but because their feelings on this feeds their sense of identity and capacity for action, they will dive head first into and cling to it. At best, you might be able to have something like civil conversation with them-hell, the Fire-touched <i>love</i> it when you buy into that -but at the end of the day, these are people who would gladly support action to kill you because it makes them feel good and right and in a place they belong that is them and theirs if they weren't werewolves for anything any reasonable and rational person would clearly see as <i>wrong</i>-and since they <i>are</i> werewolves, they don't just have to support it, they can and will take action to those ends.<br /> <br /> That the Forsaken also kill humans and willfully shape territories in ways that is demonstrably monstrous does not make the Pure an equal form of evil to them. They clearly embody ideologies and practices that are far more reprehensible than the murky waters the Forsaken exist and act in.<br /> <br /> The only decent Pure is an Uratha who <i>stops being a Pure</i>. Anything else is just killing you with a smile.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hear you.<br /> Let me just point out that while I feel that there could be Pure that are also decent people, they should not be common. They should be rare. They should be the exception, not the rule.<br /> In my opinion, the point of the presence of decent anshega is not necessarily to make a point that these characters can exist (though you could do that), but rather to provide questions about what matters to the PC's.<br /> Killing the decent Pure would be the right thing to do in many people's opinion, they are still Pure &amp; thus the enemy. On the other hand, killing such people might be against your morality.<br /> If follow your morality &amp; let them live you could be ending up with some unusual &amp; unconventional allies. The flipside of this is what will the opinion of the greater werewolf community be.<br /> <br /> Anyway, if you don't like the idea of decent people from the (as you call them) Antagonist Organizations, just don't use them. Simple as that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T23:16:06-07:00","id":1383516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1382725-decent-anshega?p=1383508#post1383508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like this misses the forest for the trees.<br /> <br /> Broadly speaking, the franchise's use of monsters as a lens for humanity tends to mean that the individual character types are kind of default sort of grey as that entire moral black and white morality scale goes, with individual players deciding how to brighten up or darken down on their deicisons, which often sets a tone for the conflict.<br /> <br /> As a result of that grey nature to of everything, larger organizations of the monsters tend to conglomerate around those grey concepts, mixtures of positives that are also paired with negatives that reflect the thematic concerns and common answers to those concerns in a way that are