ral and ethical standing, and often they don't appeal to rational argumentation.<br /> <br /> The Pure are werewolves motivated by hatred of the world and what they got, they hearken back to a myth that doesn't reflect the realities of either the present or the days those myths took place in because it gives them a feeling of power and place. They are motivated by a sense that civilization has castrated them, that their racial superiority and purity is being defiled by interbreeding, that their religions justify their violence against an unworthy and unenlightened mass. These things will never make logical or rational sense, and certainly defy any sense of actual moral or ethical consideration, but because their feelings on this feeds their sense of identity and capacity for action, they will dive head first into and cling to it. At best, you might be able to have something like civil conversation with them-hell, the Fire-touched <i>love</i> it when you buy into that -but at the end of the day, these are people who would gladly support action to kill you because it makes them feel good and right and in a place they belong that is them and theirs if they weren't werewolves for anything any reasonable and rational person would clearly see as <i>wrong</i>-and since they <i>are</i> werewolves, they don't just have to support it, they can and will take action to those ends.<br /> <br /> That the Forsaken also kill humans and willfully shape territories in ways that is demonstrably monstrous does not make the Pure an equal form of evil to them. They clearly embody ideologies and practices that are far more reprehensible than the murky waters the Forsaken exist and act in.<br /> <br /> The only decent Pure is an Uratha who <i>stops being a Pure</i>. Anything else is just killing you with a smile.</div> </div> </div> </div>All true, but in your explaination you consider the Pure tribe as a unified set of ideology.<br /> It is like to say that all catholic cristians follow ALL the rules andideologies of their creed.<br /> What i m triyng to say is that as tribe are fundamentally a form of religion, and you can have different level of adherence.<br /> So you can also have Pures that embrace some belief of the tribe but not others, or reluctant tribe members.<br /> Of course this is the kind of pure who rarely reach high ranks in the tribe, and other pack members could frequently keep an eye on him for signs of defect.<br /> But unlike the Hosts, who are &quot;evil&quot; by nature, werewolf can choose how much &quot;evil&quot; they are day by day.<br /> As an example it comes to my mind Stroheim, from JoJo series 2","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24346,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","user":"Neos01","date":". 04-24-2020, 02:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T23:49:37-07:00","id":1383521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1382725-decent-anshega?p=1383516#post1383516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But unlike the Hosts, who are &quot;evil&quot; by nature, werewolf can choose how much &quot;evil&quot; they are day by day</div> </div> </div> </div>The Pure Tribes have bound their souls to hateful ancient godlings that embody suffering, disease, and brutal nature even before their more personal fealty to pettier tyrants that don't have Father Wolf's kids' tenuous line on being more than the sum of their terrible parts. They did this because they wanted to, because they hated stuff about the world, and they were prepared to be flayed or burned or worse to express that hatred in an irreversible manner.<br /> <br /> This is not just a matter of beliefs \u2014 being sworn to a Pure Firstborn and belonging to a Pure pack is a metaphysical state with consequences. The Aspirations and Bans imposed by the kinds of spirits that lend their patronage to the Pure are not going to be great even before getting into what their tribal oaths encourage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 04-24-2020, 02:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T23:49:48-07:00","id":1383522,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure in Shunned by the Moon there's a section entitled &quot;Tribe Over All&quot; in the proper Pure Tribes write up for WtF 2E that specifically highlights how the Pure Tribes are far more fanatical and hardlined in their dedication to their Tribal oaths and culture. (Primarily because they have no Auspice to draw from so their sole source of power and protection would come from either their Tribal Firstborn or Pack Totem, hence why Tribe dogma would be so much more important to them.)<br /> <br /> Granted there is merit to building the person first before the werewolf but, much like the benevolent Seer argument, if you are to use that angle and not soften the Pure Tribes for your own specific chronicle then they would need to be close to being outcasts from within their own territory. Either remaining in the Tribe because they're too powerful (for whatever reason) to be removed or too valuable to get rid off. The more they cling to (the human's) morality then the more alienated they would become within the eyes of their more &quot;enlightened&quot; Tribemates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T01:13:14-07:00","id":1383529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1382725-decent-anshega?p=1383521#post1383521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Pure Tribes have bound their souls to hateful ancient godlings that embody suffering, disease, and brutal nature even before their more personal fealty to pettier tyrants that don't have Father Wolf's kids' tenuous line on being more than the sum of their terrible parts. They did this because they wanted to, because they hated stuff about the world, and they were prepared to be flayed or burned or worse to express that hatred in an irreversible manner.<br /> <br /> This is not just a matter of beliefs \u2014 being sworn to a Pure Firstborn and belonging to a Pure pack is a metaphysical state with consequences. The Aspirations and Bans imposed by the kinds of spirits that lend their patronage to the Pure are not going to be great even before getting into what their tribal oaths encourage.</div> </div> </div> </div>So if i understand it correctly you are saying that joining a tribe metaphisically change your behaviour and that in the case of pure tribes the change is even more deep?<br /> There are reference of this in the books?<br /> <br /> Let s make an example:<br /> A ivory claw leader who believe strongly in the cause has a son, who undergoes first change.<br /> The son doesn t embrace the father beliefs so strongly because he doesn t think that superiority give you the right to kill inferiors, but he doesn t want to disappoint his mother, so he join the tribe.<br /> Would the joining make him more in line with the tribe creed, raising his bloodlust for enemies or he would remain a reluctant Ivory claw?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T06:46:23-07:00","id":1383591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1382725-decent-anshega?p=1383516#post1383516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All true, but in your explaination you consider the Pure tribe as a unified set of ideology.<br /> It is like to say that all catholic cristians follow ALL the rules andideologies of their creed.<br /> What i m triyng to say is that as tribe are fundamentally a form of religion, and you can have different level of adherence.<br /> So you can also have Pures that embrace some belief of the tribe but not others, or reluctant tribe members.<br /> Of course this is the kind of pure who rarely reach high ranks in the tribe, and other pack members could frequently keep an eye on him for signs of defect.<br /> But unlike the Hosts, who are &quot;evil&quot; by nature, werewolf can choose how much &quot;evil&quot; they are day by day.<br /> As an example it comes to my mind Stroheim, from JoJo series 2</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Like, I dunno, calling themselves the Pure and having their own Oath they all adhere to?<br /> <br /> 2)No, it's like saying all Christian Extremists* swear by a root perception on reality that has no business influencing modern society since We Know Things Now regardless of the fact that some of them debate on whether they should kill Jews or Gays first.<br /> <br /> 3)You made a pact with an entity that made a fundamental change to your nature (In that now your Harmony slides more out of whack if you disregard the Tribal Ban) with a gibbering diseeased prophet hunt god, a racial-purity obsessed torture-hunt god, and a &quot;Human civilization is a mistake I am more than happy to correct&quot; hunt god. That's the base level of adherence of the Pure at any and all times, and you'll forgive me if I don't care how many kittens they go pulling out of trees, because <i>that is not a thing a good person does</i>.<br /> <br /> 4) Day by day choices do not stop those choices being slanted by the hatred that motivated them to bind their essences to the afore mentioned gods that changed their metaphysical makeup. That a Fire-Touched is merely voting in the neighborhood council rather than slitting someone's throat one day does not mean that they aren't going to use that vote to increase the Supremacy of the Shadow over the Flesh for reasons that are Bad and end effects down the road that are bad.<br /> <br /> Point is, yes, not every Pure's moment is going to be filling the world with plague and suffering and hunger and hatred-assumedly they gotta have days off work too, and days where they aren't that all into their work. This does not stop the fact that the Pure as a whole are unquestionably an evil organization by contrast to the murkier Forsaken Tribes, that the majority of it's members at some point in their time with them decided to buy into the pitch, and that the most decent members of the Anshega are those who're questioning the pacts they made-the sort of Anshega who are flirting with the idea of No Longer Being Pure.<br /> <br /> Which I should note is Not An Easy Process.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1382725-decent-anshega?p=1383529#post1383529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So if i understand it correctly you are saying that joining a tribe metaphisically change your behaviour and that in the case of pure tribes the change is even more deep?<br /> There are reference of this in the books?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Tribal Oath is added to you list of Things that cause Harmony to go one way(Tribal Oaths are considered part of the Oath of the Moon/Urfarah, which breaks towards Flesh). So yes, it changes your metaphysical nature, and as a result, it changes your behavior.<br /> <br /> *Let's be generous and go that route.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 04-24-2020, 10:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T07:27:28-07:00","id":1383597,"title":"","content":"Reading the &quot;tribe over all&quot; section mentioned by Dusksage and the rules on Harmony mentioned by ArcaneArts i must admit that i ve changed my mind.<br /> The child of my previous example would most probably never enter the tribe, failing the rite of initiation for lack of dedication and would probably end up being slain by his mother as a result!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24346,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","user":"Neos01","date":". 04-24-2020, 10:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T08:05:40-07:00","id":1383603,"title":"","content":"I think you're making it more difficult for yourself by looking at this from the perspective of a ST. It won't matter how nice you make your NPCs if it's not evident to your players; so you only really need to make them act 'decently' around the players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T11:12:59-07:00","id":1383633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1382725-decent-anshega?p=1383603#post1383603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you're making it more difficult for yourself by looking at this from the perspective of a ST.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is sort of an issue with a lot of the 'they're evil.' statements in Werewolf. We have the benefit of not being chosen at random (presumably by the moon god) to be fleshwarping horrors who are obsessed with the hunt to the point that resistance leads to abomination. We also have the benefit of not being forced to live in a world where spirits have a constant push on our souls and way of life. We are also human, and so a lot of views on the forum revolve around 'if its bad for humans, it's objectively bad.<br /> <br /> But werewolves don't get to live metalives where they can flip through Dark Eras and see that the silver bane existed before the fall of Pangaea, or know what Pangaea was like. And while we can slap the labels of disease and torture and anti-civilization on the Pure Firstborn (in case you need some extra incentive to thinking they're bad) they also revolve around truth and religion, nobility, and the natural cycle of life and death. If you wanted to go farther you could also note that freshly changed werewolves don't get a copy of the corebook, and when hearing about the Forsaken Totems they might not think that they're the 'good ones' something that people approaching the game have had issue with. Because they aren't.<br /> <br /> Also it's worth reading the second edition books. Core, the Pack, Shunned by the Moon. The Dark Eras are great too. It's not hard to find some level of decency there.<br /> <br /> From <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/playing-the-pure-werewolf-the-forsaken/\" target=\"_blank\">Playing the Pure</a>:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;The Fire-Touched hunt those who dishonor and disrespect the Shadow. Anyone who harms or tyrannizes a spirit without provocation, or who attempts to seal away the Hisil, such as by thickening the Gauntlet or closing a locus, gains the zealous hatred of the Izidakh. This may include unwitting humans who disrespect icons or idols representing spirits. Disrespect to Luna and her servants doesn\u2019t earn the Fire-Touched\u2019s enmity, of course.<br /> <br /> The Ivory Claws hunt those who dishonor their lineage. Those who break family traditions, or who defy their elders without pure reason are targets of the Tzuumfin. This runs both ways. The Ivory Claws won\u2019t tolerate parents who weaken the bloodline by blocking strong mates for their offspring, or who heap scorn and degradation on their children and manipulate them into failing their lineage. The Tzuumfin consider all Forsaken to have dihonored their obligations to Urfarah, and are all valid prey for their hunts.<br /> <br /> The Predator Kings hunt those who fail to honor the hunt. Humans who don\u2019t hunt at least once per season, or those who try to end hunting are the Predator Kings\u2019 prey, as are werewolves who break off the Sacred Hunt. The Ninna Farakh don\u2019t automatically target those who kill for sport instead of sustenance, but their must be purpose behind a hunt for it have honor. Feeding, honing or teaching skills, or culling an overgrown population are valid reasons. Killing for simple fun is not. The Predator Kings sometimes forgive questionable hunts that used primitive or natural weaponry, but disrespectful hunts conducted with modern, high-powered weapons are never tolerated.&quot; </div> </div> </div>Just like you can have a zealous inquisitor, a madman hunting for vengeance for centuries old deeds, or the crew from the Hills Have Eyes, you can have shamans taking down spirit-enslavers, blood hunters busting abusive parents, and metropolitan party girls who bring down folks who pay just to hunt drugged animals just to have photo-ops. And you can do all these things as Forsaken as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T11:30:28-07:00","id":1383635,"title":"","content":"And I feel like dealing in moral absolutes kind of defeats the &quot;this is what things are locally&quot; vibe that a lot of 2nd Edition tries to do with things. Global organizations and broad strokes are fine to categorize at a glance, but dealing with things on a person-to-person basis has a lot of variability in what happens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25423-voytek","name":"Voytek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25423_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T12:38:54-07:00","id":1383656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1382725-decent-anshega?p=1383529#post1383529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if i understand it correctly you are saying that joining a tribe metaphisically change your behaviour and that in the case of pure tribes the change is even more deep?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm saying that, in addition to the specific adjustment to your Harmony the tribal ban applies, Pure werewolves belong to Pure packs with totems of the sort that support the Pure's ideology, which gives them an Aspiration and Ban in line with those kinds of spirits.<br /> <br /> It is literally more difficult, socially, to talk a werewolf into doing something that conflicts with their pack's Aspiration, and a pack Ban goes from elective to imposed very quickly considering the first breach starts applying penalties and the second breach removes Totem dots in a way that could very easily end up with angry werewolves and a powerful spirit on your case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T12:44:22-07:00","id":1383658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1382725-decent-anshega?p=1383591#post1383591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the most decent members of the Anshega are those who're questioning the pacts they made-the sort of Anshega who are flirting with the idea of No Longer Being Pure.<br /> <br /> Which I should note is Not An Easy Process.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always wondered about this, especially in 2e. Like, obviously, the correct answer is &quot;one stops being Pure by doing whatever is most interesting for your story,&quot; but I feel like there are a lot of interesting mechanical questions born of the metaphysics of what comes <i>after</i> one makes that choice.<br /> <br /> It's unlikely that a former Pure [newly Impure?] can regain their Auspice short of plot, so what happens when they can't? Do they simply become sadder Ghost Wolves? Can they join a Forsaken Tribe, and if so, how would their Hunter's Aspect change? Can they even remove the influence of the Pure Firstborn that once filled their soul? How do they gain new dots of Renown now that Lunes and the Pure spirit totems refuse to recognize their deeds? Can they gain new dots of Renown at all?<br /> <br /> There probably aren't any correct answers to these questions except which make for the most interesting story, but it's fun to think about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Posting gives me anxiety, but I'm still happy to be here</i><br /> Habitual Lurker, Vengrel Liker, Acolyte Apologist, She/Her","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25955-somethingfishy","name":"SomethingFishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25955_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T14:33:22-07:00","id":1383670,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25955-somethingfishy\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25955_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25955\" data-vbnamecard=\"25955\">SomethingFishy</a> maybe they could go on a quest into the Shadow to regain their Auspice? Or try to bargain with a (relatively) sane Lune?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T17:47:29-07:00","id":1383695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1382725-decent-anshega?p=1383633#post1383633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is sort of an issue with a lot of the 'they're evil.' statements in Werewolf. We have the benefit of not being chosen at random (presumably by the moon god) to be fleshwarping horrors who are obsessed with the hunt to the point that resistance leads to abomination. We also have the benefit of not being forced to live in a world where spirits have a constant push on our souls and way of life. We are also human, and so a lot of views on the forum revolve around 'if its bad for humans, it's objectively bad.<br /> <br /> But werewolves don't get to live metalives where they can flip through Dark Eras and see that the silver bane existed before the fall of Pangaea, or know what Pangaea was like. And while we can slap the labels of disease and torture and anti-civilization on the Pure Firstborn (in case you need some extra incentive to thinking they're bad) they also revolve around truth and religion, nobility, and the natural cycle of life and death. If you wanted to go farther you could also note that freshly changed werewolves don't get a copy of the corebook, and when hearing about the Forsaken Totems they might not think that they're the 'good ones' something that people approaching the game have had issue with. Because they aren't.<br /> <br /> Also it's worth reading the second edition books. Core, the Pack, Shunned by the Moon. The Dark Eras are great too. It's not hard to find some level of decency there.<br /> <br /> From <a href=\"http://&quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/playing-the-pure-werewolf-the-forsaken/&quot;]Playing</a> the Pure[/URL]:<br /> <br /> <br /> Just like you can have a zealous inquisitor, a madman hunting for vengeance for centuries old deeds, or the crew from the Hills Have Eyes, you can have shamans taking down spirit-enslavers, blood hunters busting abusive parents, and metropolitan party girls who bring down folks who pay just to hunt drugged animals just to have photo-ops. And you can do all these things as Forsaken as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Arguing moral ambiguity based on metanarrative character creation choices versus in-character narrative choices doesn't change the fact the Pure Tribes are written as openly antagonistic to both the Forsaken Tribes and baseline human society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":". 04-24-2020, 09:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T01:30:28-07:00","id":1383734,"title":"","content":"Hi this is the creator of this thread.<br /> So in the whole Chronicles of Darkness setting is one of choice, as in you choose what to use. What mechanics, what creatures, what characters, what concepts, etc.<br /> This thread is kinda just adding to that. Decent Anshega is a concept which you can use if the urge strikes you, but you don't have to use it if you don't want to.<br /> Me? I like the moral ambiguity the concept brings in, with bad guys part of &quot;Protagonist Organizations&quot; &amp; good guys part of &quot;Antagonist Organizations&quot;.<br /> If you don't like that that's ok, but please stop trying to convince everyone else of what you believe in.<br /> <br /> Also I'm getting the impression that some of the people here believe that &quot;antagonist&quot; means &quot;villain&quot;. It doesn't. Antagonist here means &quot;a person who actively opposes or is hostile to someone or something&quot; there is nothing there that demands an antagonist be a baddie.<br /> I'm sorry if my assumption here offended anyone.<br /> <br /> Now, I think I've given the best arguments in support of the concept of Decent Anshega that I can come up with &amp; if they don't make people happy nothing will. So I'm gonna duck out of this argument &amp; basically not argue my point anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T09:56:54-07:00","id":1383785,"title":"","content":"Ah, I see. There may have been some confusion on my part. I was under the impression this was a proof of concept discussion rather than a straight idea page.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T11:06:37-07:00","id":1383801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krat05</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1382725-decent-anshega?p=1383734#post1383734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi this is the creator of this thread.<br /> So in the whole Chronicles of Darkness setting is one of choice, as in you choose what to use. What mechanics, what creatures, what characters, what concepts, etc.<br /> This thread is kinda just adding to that. Decent Anshega is a concept which you can use if the urge strikes you, but you don't have to use it if you don't want to.<br /> Me? I like the moral ambiguity the concept brings in, with bad guys part of &quot;Protagonist Organizations&quot; &amp; good guys part of &quot;Antagonist Organizations&quot;.<br /> If you don't like that that's ok, but please stop trying to convince everyone else of what you believe in.<br /> <br /> Also I'm getting the impression that some of the people here believe that &quot;antagonist&quot; means &quot;villain&quot;. It doesn't. Antagonist here means &quot;a person who actively opposes or is hostile to someone or something&quot; there is nothing there that demands an antagonist be a baddie.<br /> I'm sorry if my assumption here offended anyone.<br /> <br /> Now, I think I've given the best arguments in support of the concept of Decent Anshega that I can come up with &amp; if they don't make people happy nothing will. So I'm gonna duck out of this argument &amp; basically not argue my point anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's disregard, then, the fact that the Pure are religious extremists, racist social movers, and misanthropic terrorists.<br /> <br /> In the vein of a decent Anshega, I'll admit I've long wanted to run a game of Forsaken where one of the packs around you that you oppose is Pure and led by a Fire-touched, but actually is probably one of your better neighbors-the Fire-touched in question is realistically playing the long game with trying to convert the player group in, but is pretty mindful of the players territories, collaborates with them on prey that fits their interests (Like taking on Azlu or going after more off-the-chain Ivory Claws) and is willing to create opportunities for them both to mutually grow their territories and resources. You know, play a &quot;good face&quot; for the Anshega by being a usually reliable ally.<br /> <br /> Now mind you, this falls under my advice is that the only good Pure is one who's questioning being a Pure-the Fire-Touched in question is supposed to be someone the players could persuade away from being Pure, and depending on how much his pack respects him (which will also be affected by players choice), maybe some of the others too. THere'd be a point in the chronicle where the line would come, where action against the player pack is expected, and how the players decided to go after it would result in either them defecting and leading a combined stand against another, more powerful pack of Pure....or a situation where-in it seems like business as usual with these guys only to confront plague and fervor at a critical juncture.<br /> <br /> Nofather points out something interesting where the interests of the Pure DO sometimes align with most people's senses of moral and ethical action, and there's a lot of room to mine that perspective-but I feel like the important key for that is that players should also be able to use those actionable sort of motives and actions to leverage the Pure away from the Oath of Urfarah. I'm not personally very keen on the idea of action and portrayal leaning a little too far into &quot;Maybe they have a point&quot;-where the Pure have a point, the Forsaken should be able to leverage that right back into their (admittedly) mixed ethos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T13:12:50-07:00","id":1383828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1382725-decent-anshega?p=1383670#post1383670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> maybe they could go on a quest into the Shadow to regain their Auspice? Or try to bargain with a (relatively) sane Lune?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they definitely could try, and either would make for an interesting story, whether or not they succeed. I'm personally inclined to believe that it's so vanishingly rare to reclaim a lost Auspice as to be functionally impossible, but when it comes to player characters and telling a good story, well, then the former Pure might just achieve the impossible.<br /> <br /> Like, imagine a pack of Forsaken player characters protecting an ally turned friend, aiding them on a mad quest into the Deep Shadow for a Lune the pack petitioned on the former Pure's behalf. What happens if their friend succeeds, proving their worth? Does the twice Forsaken gain a new Auspice then and there? Does it happen sometime within the month, like a second First Change? If so, what is that even like when you're already an Uratha?<br /> <br /> But I think that line of thought drifts increasingly further from the topic of decent Anshega.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Posting gives me anxiety, but I'm still happy to be here</i><br /> Habitual Lurker, Vengrel Liker, Acolyte Apologist, She/Her","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25955-somethingfishy","name":"SomethingFishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25955_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T16:40:45-07:00","id":1383861,"title":"","content":"Well let's look at this way<br /> <br /> The Pure, when you take what they are as a whole, cant be decent, as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> has already pointed out. The fire touched will always believe in their blind worship and stick to spirits who have a morality even more twisted than theirs, the Ivory Claws will always hate you for being &quot;impure&quot;, and the predator kings will kill you for simply not respecting their idea of the hunt and even use of technology.<br /> <br /> But, and I am using tv tropes lingo here, but Evil Virtues can be found in the Aneshega<br /> <br /> The Fire Touched believe in (their own version) redemption of the forsaken and will try very hard to turn them to their side rather than kill them. They will also fight to the death to protect the misuse of spirits, which means Forsaken alliances arent unrealistic. Not common, but more than possible still.<br /> <br /> The Predator Kings, as bloodthirsty and flawed their methods are, wish for a time nature ruled supreme. They genuinely wish there were no deforestation or any of that, and believe a pure state of predator and prey and the hunt. And despite how they are, they will respect anyone who adheres to the hunt and old ways. Even a mere human (admittedly, I have a hard time with the predator kings)<br /> <br /> The Ivory Claws, and this is pretty difficult because they really are the nazis of werewolves, are nonetheless honor bound and are (quite ironically) in touch with their human side. When an ivory claw makes a promise, he is expected to keep it, and if his family is dishonoured, he will correct that slight. And despite having the most bitter hatred, they know when to negotiate (correct me if I'm wrong anyone, but i believe in either corebook or The Pack, its Ivory Claws who managed to put together a protectorate with the Forsaken)<br /> <br /> So, while the Pure will never, ever be decent by our standards (and I'm pretty sure Forsaken standards), they can have traits that can at least give you a begrudging respect for them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T18:22:24-07:00","id":1383884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1382725-decent-anshega?p=1383695#post1383695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arguing moral ambiguity based on metanarrative character creation choices versus in-character narrative choices doesn't change the fact the Pure Tribes are written as openly antagonistic to both the Forsaken Tribes and baseline human society.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't say they weren't. They're an antagonist faction, that's a given. But a faction is a whole, and individuals can vary. It's why we have examples across both editions of Predator Kings that are modern jet setting party girls and corporate sharks who drive a BMW to work every morning. An oath to 'honor nothing of human craft' does not mean 'every Predator King is a wanton maniac who ceaselessly runs around killing innocent people for living in a house.' And whatever label you want to slap on a tribe, a ST can whip up members to stand out as different among them, or might already appear in the books.<br /> <br /> Them being antagonists doesn't mean they fit some objective form of morality (such as our 'if it's detrimental to humanity, it's bad' view which is entirely subjective).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T19:38:43-07:00","id":1383897,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25955-somethingfishy\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25955_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25955\" data-vbnamecard=\"25955\">SomethingFishy</a> brilliant! I love it \ud83d\ude0a.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24173\" data-vbnamecard=\"24173\">Primordial newcomer</a> in Dark Eras Companion Forsaken by Rome the Ivory Claws and the Iron Masters work together to establish the Romulan Protectorate which claims dominion over all Uratha and spirits within the Roman Empire. They oppose the Blood Talons, Bone Shadows and Predator Kings who live in Germania beyond the Rhine. The Ivory Claws marry into the old patrician families and the Iron Masters are allied with the rising plebeian class.<br /> <br /> Have you guys read Savage Age? How are the Predator Kings related to the Naghaluu (sp?), the Dire Wolves of the Paleolithic period?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-25T20:40:00-07:00","id":1383902,"title":"","content":"Unsurprisingly, I\u2019m a fan of 2e\u2019s increased local focus and lack of homogeneity for tribes. The Pure tribes are antagonists and their philosophies are more alien to what we find acceptable as humans. But, to try and answer the thread\u2019s title, what does \u2018decent\u2019 mean? If by decent you mean \u2018Anshega who seem reasonable and willing to engage with outside ideas and not just murder everyone\u2019, then the answer is yes. But if decent means \u2018like human philosophies and morals\u2019 then no - but neither are the Forsaken.<br /> <br /> Something I *really* like in 2e is that the Pure are more in control of what does and doesn\u2019t make the grade of their philosophies on a very personal level. The Fire-Touched revere spirits, but they hunt those who disrespect the Shadow. For some, this includes hunting spirits who think they should spend their time in the Flesh. That\u2019s disrespecting the Shadow and spirits who think Fire-Touched are automatically pushovers are in for a rude shock. Ivory Claws value respecting lineages and family. On one extreme this can be eugenic-level bullshit, on the other end it\u2019s just families working together to make themselves the strongest they can be against the world. Predator Kings honour the hunt. Some are barbarians who live in the wilderness, make all their own things and hunt down any humans who come into their territories. Others accept that the hunt can mean more than blood and meat and grudgingly accept that humans have adapted their hunts to modern life. The Predator Kings hate it but they live with it.<br /> <br /> But no Anshega is going to be 100% decent by human standards. By simply being Uratha they\u2019re content to kill humans without dwelling on it so much. They\u2019ll follow old spirit laws that call for blood and pain because that\u2019s their culture. They\u2019ll use strength and magic to dominate and overwhelm resistance without worrying about broader society because that\u2019s what their ancient instincts tell them. <br /> <br /> The thing is, this also applies to the Forsaken. Very few of them are \u2018decent\u2019 by human standards. Maybe none. Some of the tribes aren\u2019t particularly aligned with human ideals, and practically none of the Auspices are. Irraka are always thinking about how they\u2019d murder you. Ithaeur care more for the invisible spirits that you have no awareness of. Etc.<br /> <br /> But anyway, the short version of it is that tribes - Anshega or Urdaga - are global concepts with local realisations. Can there be decent Anshega? Certainly. Can there be monstrous Urdaga that make the Pure look moderate? Absolutely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T00:41:53-07:00","id":1383920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1382725-decent-anshega?p=1383902#post1383902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unsurprisingly, I\u2019m a fan of 2e\u2019s increased local focus and lack of homogeneity for tribes. The Pure tribes are antagonists and their philosophies are more alien to what we find acceptable as humans. But, to try and answer the thread\u2019s title, what does \u2018decent\u2019 mean? If by decent you mean \u2018Anshega who seem reasonable and willing to engage with outside ideas and not just murder everyone\u2019, then the answer is yes. But if decent means \u2018like human philosophies and morals\u2019 then no - but neither are the Forsaken.<br /> <br /> Something I *really* like in 2e is that the Pure are more in control of what does and doesn\u2019t make the grade of their philosophies on a very personal level. The Fire-Touched revere spirits, but they hunt those who disrespect the Shadow. For some, this includes hunting spirits who think they should spend their time in the Flesh. That\u2019s disrespecting the Shadow and spirits who think Fire-Touched are automatically pushovers are in for a rude shock. Ivory Claws value respecting lineages and family. On one extreme this can be eugenic-level bullshit, on the other end it\u2019s just families working together to make themselves the strongest they can be against the world. Predator Kings honour the hunt. Some are barbarians who live in the wilderness, make all their own things and hunt down any humans who come into their territories. Others accept that the hunt can mean more than blood and meat and grudgingly accept that humans have adapted their hunts to modern life. The Predator Kings hate it but they live with it.<br /> <br /> But no Anshega is going to be 100% decent by human standards. By simply being Uratha they\u2019re content to kill humans without dwelling on it so much. They\u2019ll follow old spirit laws that call for blood and pain because that\u2019s their culture. They\u2019ll use strength and magic to dominate and overwhelm resistance without worrying about broader society because that\u2019s what their ancient instincts tell them. <br /> <br /> The thing is, this also applies to the Forsaken. Very few of them are \u2018decent\u2019 by human standards. Maybe none. Some of the tribes aren\u2019t particularly aligned with human ideals, and practically none of the Auspices are. Irraka are always thinking about how they\u2019d murder you. Ithaeur care more for the invisible spirits that you have no awareness of. Etc.<br /> <br /> But anyway, the short version of it is that tribes - Anshega or Urdaga - are global concepts with local realisations. Can there be decent Anshega? Certainly. Can there be monstrous Urdaga that make the Pure look moderate? Absolutely.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's ok, I have a question regarding more moderate Ivory Claws. Their Oath means that all forsaken, by being forsaken, fit their description of Sacred Prey. How do moderate Ivory Claws tend to interact with them, especially since Ivory Claws can be surprisingly diplomatic","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T00:57:28-07:00","id":1383922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1382725-decent-anshega?p=1383920#post1383920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it's ok, I have a question regarding more moderate Ivory Claws. Their Oath means that all forsaken, by being forsaken, fit their description of Sacred Prey. How do moderate Ivory Claws tend to interact with them, especially since Ivory Claws can be surprisingly diplomatic</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m sorry, I don\u2019t quite understand your question? How do moderate Ivory Claws interact with whom? And the second part of your question answers the first, \u2018they can be surprisingly diplomatic\u2019. What am I not understanding here?<br /> <br /> Addressing the foundation of the question - the Ivory Claw oath doesn\u2019t automatically encompass the Forsaken, most just interpret it so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T03:56:26-07:00","id":1383935,"title":"","content":"Nvm \u263a\ufe0f. I forgot Savage Age is for WoD Werewolf, not CoD Werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T12:03:24-07:00","id":1383987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1382725-decent-anshega?p=1383922#post1383922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I\u2019m sorry, I don\u2019t quite understand your question? How do moderate Ivory Claws interact with whom? And the second part of your question answers the first, \u2018they can be surprisingly diplomatic\u2019. What am I not understanding here?<br /> <br /> Addressing the foundation of the question - the Ivory Claw oath doesn\u2019t automatically encompass the Forsaken, most just interpret it so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry for the lack of clarity. I meant to ask, how do moderate Ivory Claws tend to regard Forsaken? Are they generally hostile toward them, do they see then as misled?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T14:35:32-07:00","id":1384024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krat05</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1382725-decent-anshega?p=1383734#post1383734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also I'm getting the impression that some of the people here believe that &quot;antagonist&quot; means &quot;villain&quot;. It doesn't. Antagonist here means &quot;a person who actively opposes or is hostile to someone or something&quot; there is nothing there that demands an antagonist be a baddie.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is factually untrue. You didn't read ArcaneArts's post correctly. An &quot;antagonist organization&quot; <i>here</i> is an organization in CofD rules as an example of how the fundamental creature of the gameline, in this case werewolves, can go &quot;too far&quot; and leave moral ambiguity behind for a clear moral failure. In this case, you are correct that the term &quot;antagonist&quot; is being hijacked. An antagonist in the more formal sense is <i>not</i> your definition, though: an antagonist in a story is specifically someone who opposes the protagonist.<br /> <br /> In other words, an antagonist fundamentally cannot exist without a protagonist. And a protagonist cannot exist without a story. In thematic terms, characters are perspectives on a theme. A theme might be, &quot;Love conquers all,&quot; and the protagonist might say, &quot;yes,&quot; while the antagonist says, &quot;no&quot;, and the story explores who is right by highlighting the consequences of one interpretation versus the other.<br /> <br /> At your table, and in your story, it is entirely possible for the antagonist to be another Forsaken. It can be a human. These are well-established, especially in W:tF, where Blood Talons and Iron Masters explicitly consider <i>all</i> Werewolves and humans, respectively, to be acceptable prey. Hell, it can be your packmate, if your group is capable of juggling that. The limit isn't imposed by the gameline, but by your imagination and your players' consent.<br /> <br /> The moral ambiguity of the &quot;protagonist organizations&quot;, as you call them, is not in question. Indeed, that's a major thematic point in every CofD gamelne. That is crucial to ArcaneArts's point. The Forsaken aren't good guys. They're just less bad than the Pure because they have some redeeming qualities. None of the Vampire covenants are moral paragons. All of the Orders in the Mage Pentacle have explicitly called-out problems. Being the good guy is not the default playstyle for a CofD gameline.<br /> <br /> But what is the moral ambiguity that you want to actually evoke? Is that something you want help with, or something you feel you're able to help others with?<br /> <br /> For instance, is it wrong to kill a member of the Pure? The Oath of the Moon already covers that. Do we owe the Pure the time of day? Should we partner with them to stop the rampage of an idigam? Should we respect the borders of their territory? Do we respect the borders of our fellow Forsaken's territory? Should we concede some of their tenets and agree to eugenics programs? How far is too far?<br /> <br /> And that's the question. That's the game. How far <i>is</i> too far? How far do you go down that road before you become Pure? Does your packmate's hardline anti-spirit policy, because they're overreacting to Fire-Touched philosophy, also go too far? At what point does your packmate's environmentalism and distaste for civilization stop being a personal quirk and become a parroting of Dire Wolf's proclamations?<br /> <br /> If you want ways for Pure to stop being Pure, then that's something we could explore. If you want moral ambiguity, then play the game. Exploring those questions <i>is the point</i>. You don't have to, but it kinda sounds like you want to, and if you're not getting that, then it's between you and your table. People might have advice along those lines if you ask.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T14:52:33-07:00","id":1384031,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2758_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2758\" data-vbnamecard=\"2758\">Errol216</a> idc. I like the idea of Pure werewolves who stay Pure but still manage to be basically good people. They are definitely the exceptions, but they shine even brighter because they are exceptions.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26055\" data-vbnamecard=\"26055\">Krat05</a> as long as your players like them, that\u2019s what really matters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T15:06:06-07:00","id":1384037,"title":"","content":"Yeah I was never keen on the idea of things like Pure being inhuman one dimensional fanatics. I definitely can see them being antagonists with chips on their shoulders but they are people too. Its not like they are Balehounds or Black Spiral Dancers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-26T18:35:40-07:00","id":1384068,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar754_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"754\" data-vbnamecard=\"754\">Eldagusto</a> totally","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T02:20:29-07:00","id":1385043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1382725-decent-anshega?p=1383436#post1383436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They changed a bit across editions. Shifts of focus that make them less torch-bearing evil goons across the board. You can still play them that way but they're not as limited by that. As shown by the examples in the second edition books, and the Pure sections. And the <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/playing-the-pure-werewolf-the-forsaken/&amp;quot;]Playing</a> the Pure blog[/URL] which was included in a Dark Era book.</div> </div> </div> </div>So? How does that even begin to challenge my point? You can apply the same treatment to nazis, and these guys are arguably worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T02:38:34-07:00","id":1385045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1382725-decent-anshega?p=1383633#post1383633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is sort of an issue with a lot of the 'they're evil.' statements in Werewolf. We have the benefit of not being chosen at random (presumably by the moon god) to be fleshwarping horrors who are obsessed with the hunt to the point that resistance leads to abomination. We also have the benefit of not being forced to live in a world where spirits have a constant push on our souls and way of life. We are also human, and so a lot of views on the forum revolve around 'if its bad for humans, it's objectively bad.<br /> <br /> But werewolves don't get to live metalives where they can flip through Dark Eras and see that the silver bane existed before the fall of Pangaea, or know what Pangaea was like. And while we can slap the labels of disease and torture and anti-civilization on the Pure Firstborn (in case you need some extra incentive to thinking they're bad) they also revolve around truth and religion, nobility, and the natural cycle of life and death. If you wanted to go farther you could also note that freshly changed werewolves don't get a copy of the corebook, and when hearing about the Forsaken Totems they might not think that they're the 'good ones' something that people approaching the game have had issue with. Because they aren't.<br /> <br /> Also it's worth reading the second edition books. Core, the Pack, Shunned by the Moon. The Dark Eras are great too. It's not hard to find some level of decency there.<br /> <br /> From <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/playing-the-pure-werewolf-the-forsaken/&amp;quot;]Playing</a> the Pure[/URL]:<br /> <br /> <br /> Just like you can have a zealous inquisitor, a madman hunting for vengeance for centuries old deeds, or the crew from the Hills Have Eyes, you can have shamans taking down spirit-enslavers, blood hunters busting abusive parents, and metropolitan party girls who bring down folks who pay just to hunt drugged animals just to have photo-ops. And you can do all these things as Forsaken as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am a consummate believer in moral relativism and even I think this is bullshit. Yes, they revolve around religion, nobility, and the natural cycle of life and death, but not truth. I already pointed out why not truth in my first post in this thread. The religion normalizes sickness and suffering. The nobility is based on vengeance and genocide. The natural order of life and death is humanity as prey and slaves. Pointing these out is like pointing out someone rescuing a dog after burning a bus load of orphans and asking why I am slack-jawed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T02:41:41-07:00","id":1385046,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26112\" data-vbnamecard=\"26112\">Excess</a> yes, but the Nazis slaughtered millions of innocents who had no effective way of fighting back. The Pure hate people who are just as powerful as they are (the Forsaken) and are very capable of fighting back. <br /> <br /> Second, the Forsaken, like the Pure, come in all races and ethnic groups, so it\u2019s not a racial thing like it was with the Nazis. <br /> <br /> Third, I think what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26055\" data-vbnamecard=\"26055\">Krat05</a> (the OP) was trying to say was that you can take the ideologies of the three Pure tribes and sort of deconstruct them so that you keep the good parts but get rid of the genocidal hatred part. That\u2019s why I said my character would\u2019ve liked hanging out with the three decent Anshega the OP described.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T02:42:56-07:00","id":1385047,"title":"","content":"I still agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> on this issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T02:46:07-07:00","id":1385048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krat05</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1382725-decent-anshega?p=1383734#post1383734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi this is the creator of this thread.<br /> So in the whole Chronicles of Darkness setting is one of choice, as in you choose what to use. What mechanics, what creatures, what characters, what concepts, etc.<br /> This thread is kinda just adding to that. Decent Anshega is a concept which you can use if the urge strikes you, but you don't have to use it if you don't want to.<br /> Me? I like the moral ambiguity the concept brings in, with bad guys part of &amp;quot;Protagonist Organizations&amp;quot; &amp; good guys part of &amp;quot;Antagonist Organizations&amp;quot;.<br /> If you don't like that that's ok, but please stop trying to convince everyone else of what you believe in.<br /> <br /> Also I'm getting the impression that some of the people here believe that &amp;quot;antagonist&amp;quot; means &amp;quot;villain&amp;quot;. It doesn't. Antagonist here means &amp;quot;a person who actively opposes or is hostile to someone or something&amp;quot; there is nothing there that demands an antagonist be a baddie.<br /> I'm sorry if my assumption here offended anyone.<br /> <br /> Now, I think I've given the best arguments in support of the concept of Decent Anshega that I can come up with &amp; if they don't make people happy nothing will. So I'm gonna duck out of this argument &amp; basically not argue my point anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Already know what antagonist means and I read the books, what confused me was how what you wrote didn't line up with what was in the game line. Being Pure is corruptive, if your unrealistic characters existed then they would have to leave the pure to retain their integrity. Normal integrity, not the game stat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T02:56:54-07:00","id":1385051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1382725-decent-anshega?p=1385046#post1385046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> yes, but the Nazis slaughtered millions of innocents who had no effective way of fighting back. The Pure hate people who are just as powerful as they are (the Forsaken) and are very capable of fighting back. <br /> <br /> Second, the Forsaken, like the Pure, come in all races and ethnic groups, so it\u2019s not a racial thing like it was with the Nazis. <br /> <br /> Third, I think what <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> (the OP) was trying to say was that you can take the ideologies of the three Pure tribes and sort of deconstruct them so that you keep the good parts but get rid of the genocidal hatred part. That\u2019s why I said my character would\u2019ve liked hanging out with the three decent Anshega the OP described.</div> </div> </div> </div>Addressing your points:<br /> <br /> 1. So? That is just a matter of opportunity. Would you call someone who wants eternal hell acceptable just because they don't have the opportunity? <br /> <br /> 2. So? After defeating the Forsaken the Gauntlet would be next and so would humanity. That is way worse.<br /> <br /> 3. The &quot;good&quot; parts are superficial, take out the horrid context and they are rather vague with no clear meaning. Like cherry-picking the bible to say it confirms morality. Why are we even looking to their creed for decency?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T04:37:03-07:00","id":1385057,"title":"","content":"Yes, most of the Pure are horrible people. But there are a few exceptions. You can cherry pick a few of the good traits and end up with a character who\u2019s definitely flawed but still a fundamentally decent person.<br /> <br /> Tbh I\u2019d love to run or play a Romeo and Juliet story between a Pure and a Forsaken (yes, I know about the Litany, but the relationship would start out platonic and only get romantic as it slowly deepens). That wouldn\u2019t work if the Pure guy is a total psychopath.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T04:54:27-07:00","id":1385059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1382725-decent-anshega?p=1385057#post1385057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(yes, I know about the Litany, but the relationship would start out platonic and only get romantic as it slowly deepens)</div> </div> </div> </div>The Litany\u2019s not a thing in Forsaken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T05:12:26-07:00","id":1385061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1382725-decent-anshega?p=1385048#post1385048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Already know what antagonist means and I read the books, <b>what confused me was how what you wrote didn't line up with what was in the game line</b>. Being Pure is corruptive, if your unrealistic characters existed then they would have to leave the pure to retain their integrity. Normal integrity, not the game stat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Emphasis mine, as its a curious statement to make when what you continue to write without nuance disregards what is in the game line. You make assertions as if your opinion is the only one that matters, and it isn\u2019t. I\u2019m not sure if you missed or ignored the post pointing out that your understanding appears to be very much 1st edition without recognising the evolution in 2nd edition, but your posts suggest your understanding is incomplete.<br /> <br /> Pure as tribes are inherently antagonistic to Forsaken. Pure as individuals or even regional forces are not necessarily so. You can continue to believe that being Pure is inherently corruptive and all Pure are cookie cutter villains with no nuance but that doesn\u2019t make it truth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T06:43:32-07:00","id":1385069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1382725-decent-anshega?p=1385057#post1385057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Romeo and Juliet story between a Pure and a Forsaken (yes, I know about the Litany, but the relationship would start out platonic and only get romantic as it slowly deepens). That wouldn\u2019t work if the Pure guy is a total psychopath.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oaths of Moon/Urfarah ( second is Pure version ) in 2E only points that Uratha need <i>'Cleave to Man'</i>, in manner of living in human society. Ban on inter-Uratha relationships is lifted in 2E, as there are no 'demon/spirit children' of 1E ( I even do not remember their name now, from 1E ). <b>WtF</b> 2E is even more inclusive for non-traditional romantic relationship as giving one of crucial Gifts of Change for all werewolves to be <i>Luna's Embrac</i>e, power to switch physical parts for the other sex on whim. More, 2E corebook even points possible same-sex Uratha couples where one of partners change physical sex by <i>Embrace</i> for 9 months and get pregnant to born full functional babies. ( That have higher chances to be Wolf-Blooded, but not deterministic. )<br /> <br /> You can even run <i>literal</i> Rome and Juliet story, as by <i>Forsaken by Rome</i> setting from <b>Dark Eras Companion</b>, Roman Republic and Empire were govern by Ivory Claws and Iron Masters dynasties in alliance - that gone broken near the end of Roman Empire. Venice must be so much nice place for families of Ivory Claws and Iron Masters to fight over their bitter war for over 1500 years now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Side Note: </b>I run with idea that Pure use <i>Luna's Embrace</i> power, just changed it name to <i>'Wolf's Drag'</i>, or something. It nicely solves Ivory Claws problem of 'pure breeding' dogma - the Claws couples can have heirs even if same sex - and has the same reverse psychology sense, like all Pure pointing curse of Silver coming from Luna. ( Which is not, as <i>Sundered World</i> setting from <b>Dark Eras</b> 1 points it. )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 05-01-2020, 09:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T07:23:53-07:00","id":1385074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1382725-decent-anshega?p=1385045#post1385045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am a consummate believer in moral relativism and even I think this is bullshit. Yes, they revolve around religion, nobility, and the natural cycle of life and death, but not truth. I already pointed out why not truth in my first post in this thread. The religion normalizes sickness and suffering. The nobility is based on vengeance and genocide. The natural order of life and death is humanity as prey and slaves. Pointing these out is like pointing out someone rescuing a dog after burning a bus load of orphans and asking why I am slack-jawed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Silver-wolf's nobility was a thing before he became a Pure totem, before he was twisted by his torture, and acknowledged even by the Forsaken. From Lore of the Forsaken, 'Each of Urfarah\u2019s Firstborn children was born to a different mother. Uratha legends say that among these female wolf-spirits, the most noble and regal mother bore in turn the most noble and regal child: Silver Wolf. The tales tell of a creature obsessed with keeping Pangaea pure of corrupting in\ufb02uence. Here was a silver-furred wolf Incarna so kingly in bearing that he believed he should lead the spirit wolf pack, even above Dire Wolf and Winter Wolf. Even above Urfarah himself. That was Hathis-Ur.' The entry goes on and on about his nobility before his twisting viewpoints, something understood by the Forsaken even if they are enemies.<br /> <br /> The natural order of life has nothing to do with slavery. While it certainly promotes humans as prey, the Predator Kings are, again, not going around killing everyone in the world because they're not werewolves. 'The Ninna Farakh respect hunting to teach or hone skills, or to cull an overgrown population, but despise those who hunt only for sport.' Even human hunters can earn their respect providing they embrace the cycle. This stems from Dire Wolf's being an embodiment of primordial predators and hunters.<br /> <br /> As has been pointed out, the Firstborn totems of the Pure put a piece of themselves inside every member of their tribe, bringing them closer to themselves and each other. From Shunned by the Moon, ' Carving away the Auspice brands leaves a void in the werewolf\u2019s spiritual self which the Pure Firstborn saw as an opportunity to strengthen their followers and further their goals. When a Pure swears her tribal oaths, she binds herself to her chosen patron and invites the tiniest portion of its overwhelming essence to fill the wounded gaps in her spirit. In this way each Pure further expresses her patron\u2019s nature, gaining a hunter\u2019s aspect representative of that Firstborn. When an Anshega hunts, she is an avatar of her god.'<br /> <br /> And Truth is one of the aspects of Rabid Wolf's being. Yes, while it gets twisted through all the layers of perspective between us and the world, the wolf himself is big on truth, and those layers are what adds to his other aspects, like madness. I did not say 'All Pure represent Truth,' or even just one of them, but as a tribe the Fire-Touched has a focus on truth that even shows through their ban.<br /> <br /> Your first post accused people of 'redefining what the Pure stand for' but they've always been more than a shallow handwave of evil. The books themselves have done this. That people have embraced certain condemnatory aspects of them and refused to acknowledge others just points to their doctrine not being as alien as people think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T12:18:37-07:00","id":1385105,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar156_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"156\" data-vbnamecard=\"156\">Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> thank you guys","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T13:43:03-07:00","id":1385131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1382725-decent-anshega?p=1385074#post1385074\" rel=\"nofollow\" titl